course: dictionary
lesson: 3695
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, look at the words around it, which are its context. «The next week they're on the bench outside the shop, sharing a flask of tea.» Sharing and tea on a bench point to a container for a drink, not to a science glass.
explain: Clues can also come from the words describing the thing. «A flask has two walls with almost no air between them, so heat can hardly cross.» Those words show that a flask is built to keep a drink hot or cold.
explain: Always check with a swap. If the sentence is about a science experiment, a flask is a glass container with a narrow neck. If it is about a picnic, a flask is a container that keeps drinks hot or cold. The setting tells you which meaning to choose.
fact: A flask is a container that keeps drinks hot or cold. It is also called a vacuum flask or a Thermos.
fact: In science, a flask is a glass container with a narrow neck, used in experiments.
fact: A conical flask is one kind of science flask, used to hold liquids.
fact: A flask can also be a small flat bottle for carrying a drink in your pocket.
fact: «A flask of tea» and «a vacuum flask» are common phrases. The word flask is a noun, and its plural is flasks.
exercise: «The next week they're on the bench outside the shop, sharing a flask of tea.» What is a flask in this sentence? | A kind of sandwich | *A container that keeps drinks hot | A bench outside a shop | A glass with a narrow neck for experiments
exercise: Mia is in a science lab and uses a glass container with a narrow neck to hold a liquid. What is it called? | A sandwich-case | A bandage | A truncheon | *A flask
exercise: «A flask has two walls with almost no air between them, so heat can hardly cross.» What does this tell you? | A flask is a sword | *A flask is built to keep drinks hot or cold | A flask cannot hold a drink | A flask is always cold
test: Which is a second meaning of flask? | A policeman's truncheon | A pair of handcuffs | Teapot | *A small flat bottle for carrying a drink in a pocket
test: Which of these is another name for a vacuum flask? | *Thermos | Bandage | Cutlass | Sandwich-case
exam: A scientist says, «Pour the liquid into the conical flask.» What kind of flask is it? | A vacuum flask for keeping tea hot | A pocket bottle for a drink | A picnic basket with a lid | *A glass container with a narrow neck, used in experiments
